1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,270
Let us open the hood.

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:03,680
Hermes has three layers.

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:05,866
Layer one is the interface layer.

4
00:00:05,866 --> 00:00:17,962
You either type in a full terminal interface, with multi-line editing, slash commands, history,
and streaming tool output, or you message it from chat apps through a single gateway process.

5
00:00:17,962 --> 00:00:20,679
Layer two is the agent runtime.

6
00:00:20,679 --> 00:00:22,007
This is the brain.

7
00:00:22,007 --> 00:00:33,760
It runs the conversation loop, calls more than forty tools, delegates work to isolated
sub-agents, compresses old context so long sessions never break, and tracks usage and cost.

8
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:36,079
Layer three is the state layer.

9
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:44,422
Every session, message, and memory is stored in a local database with
full-text search, so the agent can recall anything across sessions.

10
00:00:44,422 --> 00:00:45,785
Follow one message.

11
00:00:45,785 --> 00:00:47,634
You send a text on Telegram.

12
00:00:47,634 --> 00:00:56,694
The gateway routes it to your session, the runtime thinks, calls
tools, and replies, and the state layer saves everything for next time.

13
00:00:56,694 --> 00:00:59,044
One brain, many doors, total memory.

